AB  - OBJECTIVE To establish a high-performance liquid chromatography (HPLC) fingerprint and a multi-component quantification method for Qiongyu Runfei Paste,and to construct a multidimensional quality evaluation approach b. y integrating chemical pattern recognition techniques,so as to provide a reference for quality control. METHODS An Agilent Eclipse Plus C18 column(4. 6 mm × 250 mm,5 μm)was used at 30 ℃. The mobile phase consisted of acetonitrile(A)and 0. 1% phosphoric acid aqueous solution(B)with gradient elution. The flow rate was 1. 0 mL·min–1,the detection wavelength was 290 nm,and the injection volume was 10 µL. The contents of six marker compounds,namely gallic acid,neochlorogenic acid,chlorogenic acid,cryptochlorogenic acid B,cryptochlorogenic acid A,and cryptochlorogenic acid C,were determined. Using the Similarity Evaluation System for Chromatographic Fingerprint of Traditional Chinese Medicine(2012),HPLC fingerprints of 10 batches of samples were established,common peaks were identified,and similarity analysis was performed. Based on the peak areas and relative peak areas of the common fingerprint peaks,hierarchical cluster analysis(HCA),principal component analysis(PCA),and partial least squares-discriminant analysis(PLS-DA)were applied to evaluate the quality of the 10 batches of Qiongyu Runfei Paste. RESULTS A total of 15 common peaks were identified in the HPLC fingerprint of Qiongyu Runfei Paste,and six components were identified as gallic acid,neochlorogenic acid,chlorogenic acid,cryptochlorogenic acid B,cryptochlorogenic acid A,and cryptochlorogenic acid C. The similarity values of the fingerprints of all 10 batches were greater than 0. 97. HCA showed that the 10 batches could be clustered into two groups according to component content and proportion. PCA and PLS-DA further confirmed this classification and identified seven components,including chlorogenic acid,cryptochlorogenic acid A, and cryptochlorogenic acid C, as the main marker compounds contributing to inter-batch quality differences. CONCLUSION The established fingerprint and content determination methods showed high accuracy and good reproducibility. Combined with chemometric techniques,they can be used for holistic quality evaluation and control of Qiongyu Runfei Paste. © (2026), (Editorial Office of Chinese Journal of Hospital Pharmacy). All rights reserved.
