AB  - With the construction of digital projects, the Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)-based review system plays an important role in the feasibility study review of projects. Therefore, the main objective is to design a set of methods and a review system for quantifying the influence factors of feasibility study review projects based on digital technology. This is intended to address the issue in the existing project review system where the verification of influence factors mainly relies on experts' experience, making it difficult to achieve objectivity and accuracy.This technology will use Natural Language Understanding (NLU) technology to analyze the textual descriptions of project functions, identify key entities and actions, and then match them with pre-defined rule abstraction models to determine the corresponding fixed influence factors. In addition, multiple methods will be employed to quantify floating influence factors, including traditional machine learning prediction models, large language model-based semantic similarity-weighted influence factors, and generative large model-based automatic code generation evaluation.  © 2025 Author(s).
