AB  - Time series forecasting is essential for informed decision-making in financial markets, but it poses challenges due to the stochastic nature of financial data. Existing forecasting methods, including classical statistical models and machine learning approaches, often struggle with the complexities of multi-series, multi-output predictions. This paper introduces a deep learning framework, N-BEATS-GAN, which combines the strengths of Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) for risk modelling with the efficient trend predictive capabilities of the deep learning model N-BEATS. The method integrates GAN loss with the Transformation Invariant Loss function with Distance EQuilibrium (TILDE-Q) loss to address amplitude and phase distortions in time series forecasting and accelerate model convergence. A dataset derived from MSCI (Morgan Stanley Capital International) Country Index data across ten countries is used for validation. Predictive accuracy is assessed using Mean Absolute Error, Mean Squared Error, Continuous Ranked Probability Score, and a risk quantification method is proposed to evaluate the capacity to capture financial risk. Experimental results demonstrate that N-BEATS-GAN significantly outperforms StockMixer, N-BEATS, DLinear, and PAGAN in both prediction accuracy and risk quantification. N-BEATS-GAN overcomes the limitations of existing models, enabling effective multi-series, multi-output forecasting while accounting for inherent risk in financial time series, highlighting its potential to enhance forecasting and risk assessment in financial markets. © 2025 Elsevier B.V.
