AB  - In this paper, the authors propose a new approach for determining the mixture proportions of positive and negative instances in both a small set of positively labeled instances contaminated with an unknown proportion of negative instances and an unlabeled instance set with an unknown mixture of positive and negative instances. The unique advantage of this method lies in its ability to derive these proportions with a high level of accuracy by directly leveraging probability density ratio estimation. Experiments conducted on synthetic and UCI repository data demonstrate that the proposed technique can robustly estimate class-prior probabilities with greater speed and better accuracy compared to existing methods, particularly in the presence of instance number and imbalance challenges. © 2024 Elsevier B.V.
