UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105048886411?origin=resultslist
AD  - Department of Automation, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China
AB  - Federated learning enables collaborative model training without sharing raw data, but its performance degrades significantly under non-IID data. A particularly challenging case is label distribution skew, where clients have different class proportions and local updates drift away from the global objective. Existing methods such as FedProx, SCAFFOLD, FedDC, and FedDyn mitigate this issue only indirectly through regularization or variance reduction. We propose FedShift, a simple method that adds a client-specific shift to the classifier logits during local training to correct the mismatch between local and global label distributions. We show that, under label shift, this modification aligns the local optimum with the global optimum, and we further establish convergence guarantees under the strongly convex assumption. Experiments on CIFAR-10, CINIC-10, and Tiny-ImageNet show that FedShift consistently outperforms strong baselines in accuracy and improves communication efficiency by up to 4.34×. These results demonstrate that FedShift is an effective and practical solution for federated learning under label distribution skew. © 2026 IEEE.
