AD  - China Southern Power Grid Company Limited, Guangzhou, China
AD  - College of Electrical Engineering, Zhejiang University, Hangzhou, China
AB  - With the increasing penetration of renewable energy there is an urgent need to consider the influence of renewable generation forecast errors on the reserve requirement. In the paper, referring to the multi-time scale classification system for reserve resources based on their response times, a multi-time scale reserve requirement quantification method is proposed based on based on Empirical Mode Decomposition (EMD). In this method, the net load forecast error samples are decomposed into multiple fluctuation components. Based on the dominant period, the fluctuation components are subjected to envelope reconstruction, thereby quantifying the multi-time scale reserve requirement. Finally, case studies on net load forecast error curve samples are presented, and the result shows that the proposed model can effectively optimize the allocation of multitime scale reserve requirement, reduces reserve overestimation. Through the calculation of reserve requirements at various renewable penetration rate, proactive adjustments to reserve requirement can be made, guiding grid planning efforts.  © 2026 IEEE.
