AD  - University of Electronic Science and Technology of China, School of Computer Science and Engineering, Chengdu, 611731, China
AB  - The Egocentric Online Action Segmentation (EOAS) task aims to temporally segment a streaming egocentric video into a set of actions. Due to the first-person perspective views and online constraints, the EOAS task raised two intrinsic difficulties: (1) The shot movements could impact the egocentric vision and make it difficult to observe overall activities. (2) The visual signals are processed in real-time, requiring models to understand the observed visual frame without any post-contextual cues after the observed frame. To address these two problems, we proposed a novel EOAS approach named Evidential Temporal Contextualization (ETC), which consists of two key modules: (1) Context-Aggregated TRansformer that predicts and aggregates potential post context to enhance representation of frame-level features, effectively addressing the insufficient temporal contextualization in streaming videos. (2) Evidential Action Contextualization that leverages evidential deep learning to quantify the uncertainty in frame-level classification and dynamically adjust the model training and inference process accordingly. Extensive experiments on three public EOAS benchmark datasets, i.e., GTEA, EgoProceL, and EgoPER, demonstrate our proposed ETC approach outperforms recent state-of-the-art methods. Additionally, we also conduct more ablation studies and generalize our proposed ETC method to exocentric videos, furtherly prove its superiority. © 1999-2012 IEEE.
