TI  - Positive-Unlabeled Hyperspectral Image Classification using nnPU Loss and Masked Autoencoder
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 IEEE 8th International Conference on Methods and Systems of Navigation and Motion Control, MSNMC 2025 - Proceedings
DO  - 10.1109/MSNMC61130.2025.11399687
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105035836888?origin=resultslist
AD  - Institute for Applied System Analysis, Kyiv, Ukraine
AB  - Hyperspectral image classification has seen significant progress with deep learning, especially CNN- and Transformer-based architectures that capture spectral-spatial relationships. However, two fundamental challenges remain: (i) the scarcity of labeled data due to the cost of pixel-level annotation, and (ii) the difficulty of fully utilizing abundant unlabeled data without overfitting. Positive-unlabeled learning addresses these issues by exploiting unlabeled data alongside a small set of positive labels, but its accuracy depends heavily on the quality of the unlabeled samples and the precision of class prior estimation. In this work, we investigate the case where the prior is known and focus on improving representation learning within positive-unlabeled frameworks. We propose a joint masked autoencoder and positive-unlabeled learning method for hyperspectral image classification. Experimental results show that our approach achieves consistent gains over standard positive-unlabeled baselines under scenarios with limited labeled data. These results highlight the effectiveness of combining masked autoencoder-based representations with positive-unlabeled classification. Code is at: https://github.com/melalex/hsi-classification-playground  © 2025 IEEE.
