AB  - Maintaining optimal shelf inventory and product availability is critical in the contemporary retail landscape to maximise sales and customer satisfaction. The demand for service robots is increasing, but few existing works have explored retail product detection, classification, and counting on a robotic platform. This paper presents an automated, real-time system for monitoring retail products. The primary goal is to detect, classify, and count retail products on shelves to streamline inventory management and minimise stockouts. This work utilised the YOLOv8 object detection model, selected for its superior balance of speed and accuracy, and trained it on the Freiburg Groceries Dataset. The system was implemented on a robot based on ROS. The model achieved a mean Average Precision (mAP50) of 88.3%, and completed detection within 3 seconds, showcasing a robust and scalable solution for automated retail product management. © 2025 IEEE.
