AB  - The aim of this chapter is to analyse the physical and physiological responses of football players with CP in competitive matches. To achieve this, a narrative review was conducted, including the principal studies that explore the physical and physiological responses of this specific group of para-footballers. In the introduction section, the importance of analysing the match physical and physiological responses of players with CP and their implications for training, classification and competition is described. In the physical and physiological responses sections, the most relevant material and quantification methods are presented, considering the available data compiled and examined from recent literature. It is known that contextual variables can influence the match physical responses of players; therefore, these different contextual variables are taken into account. To conclude the chapter, the practical applications section is presented, along with future research needs in the field. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Iván Peña-González, Raúl Reina and Manuel Moya-Ramón; individual chapters, the contributors.
