AB  - The authors investigated the applicability of machine learning-based hammering test quantification methods to laser hammering systems. This method quantitatively evaluates the degree of defects using an anomaly detection technique with CNN (Convolutional Neural Network) features extraction from the imaged hammering sound. The quantitative evaluation and generalization performance for the conventional human hammering test sound were examined. The laser hammering system applies a high-power laser beam to the concrete surface for an extremely short period of time creating a physical impact. This technology enables hammering tests remotely and automatically. As a result of the study, it was shown that capability of quantitative evaluation of the degree of defects up to around 15mm depth using laser hammering sounds. The capacity may be modifiable with the system parameters. © 2024 International Committee of the SCMT conferences. All rights reserved.
