AD  - Aerospace Times Low Altitude Technology Co., Ltd., Chongqing, China
AB  - With the rapid proliferation of low-altitude aircraft in urban dense areas, their safety risks have become a critical constraint on industry development. Based on a four-dimensional framework encompassing technology, environment, operations, and management, this paper proposes a set of safety risk identification and classification indicator systems for low-altitude flight in urban dense areas. Through literature analysis, historical data mining, and expert assessment, we systematically identified multiple typical risk sources and revealed the chain propagation mechanisms of multi-dimensional risks. Furthermore, we constructed a three-level indicator system comprising 'Target Layer-Criterion Layer-Indicator Layer,' clarifying quantification methods and data sources. The study demonstrates that this system can provide a structured analytical tool for airspace management, route planning, and emergency response, facilitating the shift in low-altitude flight safety management from passive handling to proactive prevention and control.  © 2025 IEEE.
