TI  - LiWXAI, Interpretable and Efficient LiDAR-based Weather Condition Detection and Identification using GLCM and AI-based Methodology
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings - 2025 IEEE 21st International Conference on Intelligent Computer Communication and Processing Conference, ICCP 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ICCP68926.2025.11427153
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105036030018?origin=resultslist
AB  - This paper presents an innovative and interpretable LiDAR-based architecture for weather condition detection and identification, leveraging the Gray-Level Co-occurrence Matrix (GLCM) and a dedicated AI model. By exploiting the unique spatial characteristics of LiDAR point cloud data, the proposed approach enhances the accuracy and robustness of detecting three distinct weather conditions: clear, rainy, and foggy. The LiDAR point cloud is preprocessed and projected into a discretized map, from which GLCMs are computed and used as input for model training. In addition, interpretability is a core feature of the method, addressed through two complementary techniques. First, an ante-hoc analysis estimates the 2D conditional probability distribution of GLCM features given the weather class prior to training. Second, a post-hoc visualization is enabled via a reshaped weight map that reveals the information learned by the model. The model is evaluated on the RADIATE dataset and benchmarked against three state-of-the-art weather classifiers. Results demonstrate the effectiveness of the LiDAR-GLCM approach and its strong potential for real-time, embedded weather recognition systems. © 2025 IEEE.
