AB  - The natural visual recognition for long-tailed distribution data is a difficult problem because the classifier is more biased towards the head classes, which often results in incorrect prediction. To solve this problem, we propose a simple one-stage network by remixing features and adjusting logits (RFAL) to handle long-tailed recognition. Our method enhances the expression ability of the tail class through the effective re-organization of deep features, and reassigns the label in favor of the tail class by providing a higher weight to the tail class. Extensive experiments on three long-tailed visual recognition datasets are conducted and the comparison of the proposed network with the existing state-of-the-art networks is made. The results show the better perfromance of the proposed network in long-tailed data recognition. © 2021 IEEE.
