AB  - The proceedings contain 1084 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Machine Learning. The topics include: Efficient Optimistic Exploration in Linear-Quadratic Regulators via Lagrangian Relaxation; super-efficiency of automatic differentiation for functions defined as a minimum; a Geometric Approach to Archetypal Analysis via Sparse Projections; context-Aware Local Differential Privacy; efficient Intervention Design for Causal Discovery with Latents; the Neural Tangent Kernel in High Dimensions: Triple Descent and a Multi-Scale Theory of Generalization; rank Aggregation from Pairwise Comparisons in the Presence of Adversarial Corruptions; boosting for Control of Dynamical Systems; an Optimistic Perspective on Offline Reinforcement Learning; optimal Bounds between f-Divergences and Integral Probability Metrics; LazyIter: A Fast Algorithm for Counting Markov Equivalent DAGs and Designing Experiments; learning What to Defer for Maximum Independent Sets; invariant Risk Minimization Games; why bigger is not always better: on finite and infinite neural networks; discriminative Jackknife: Quantifying Uncertainty in Deep Learning via Higher-Order Influence Functions; frequentist Uncertainty in Recurrent Neural Networks via Blockwise Influence Functions; random extrapolation for primal-dual coordinate descent; a new regret analysis for Adam-type algorithms; restarted Bayesian Online Change-point Detector achieves Optimal Detection Delay; maximum Likelihood with Bias-Corrected Calibration is Hard-To-Beat at Label Shift Adaptation; the Implicit Regularization of Stochastic Gradient Flow for Least Squares; structural Language Models of Code; LowFER: Low-rank Bilinear Pooling for Link Prediction; discount Factor as a Regularizer in Reinforcement Learning; neuro-Symbolic Visual Reasoning: Disentangling “Visual” from “Reasoning”; the Differentiable Cross-Entropy Method; Customizing ML Predictions For Online Algorithms; fairwashing Explanations with Off-Manifold De