AB  - Positive and unlabeled (PU) learning is an important branch of semi-supervised learning. In the setting of positive and unlabeled learning, if the class prior is known, the classifier would be successfully learned. However, in practical applications, the class prior is unknown, and it can only be obtained from the PU data through the estimation method. In this paper, we proposed a novel method HDBEL (Hierarchical Division Based on Ensemble Learning) for estimating the label frequency from PU data. Label frequency serves as a proxy for the class prior. First, HDBEL algorithm looks for the attribute subdomains with large label probability through the hierarchical partition method based on ensemble learning and then estimates the lower bound of label frequency by combining with the approximation formula of Hoeffding inequality. Finally, experiments on ten benchmark datasets showed that the HDBEL algorithm had higher accuracy than the existing technical methods, and the speed is seven times higher than the TIcE algorithm. © 2020, Asian Association for Agricultural Engineering. All rights reserved.
