AB  - In this study, we have developed a framework to propagate the uncertainty from the sorption experiments to the THC model, and then to the PA model. To quantify the uncertainty in SCM parameters, we developed a Python package for the Bayesian inference and general UQ. In addition, we developed a surrogate model for the THC model to quantify the buffer-averaged Kd. The Kd values were then transferred to the PA model (PFLOTRAN) for UQ. Although the results are preliminary, they demonstrate multi-model connections and associated uncertainty quantification methodology to maximize the use of existing experimental datasets as well as more complex geochemical models than Kd-based retardation coefficients. © 2022 Proceedings of the International High-Level Radioactive Waste Management Conference, IHLRWM 2022, Embedded with the 2022 ANS Winter Meeting. All rights reserved.
