AB  - The facial nerve is an array that encompasses motor and sensory fibers. It is one of the most common cranial nerves involved in disorders that considers congenital, traumatic, inflammatory and neoplastic disorders. Facial palsy is a common disease that results from the abnormal state of the facial nerve. In order to understand the full behavior, a quantification method for facial palsy is developed. The method that we propose uses the muscle trajectory information in order to perform a comparison between the right and left side of the face starting from the sagittal plane. To obtain such information, we developed an algorithm that will read a sensor array distributed across the face in order to read the state of the muscle in real time. Moreover, a statistical analysis is performed allowing us to know the state of the facial nerve. Accurate facial palsy measurement are key in the disorder treatment. According to the results found by our system, healthy faces must show a high correlation as well as a large standard deviation, correlation coefficient and a statistical mean. © 2021 American Institute of Physics Inc.. All rights reserved.
