AB  - This introductory chapter presents some of the main paradigms of intelligent data analysis provided by machine learning and data mining. After discussing several types of learning (supervised, unsupervised, semi-supervised, active and reinforcement learning) we examine several classes of learning algorithms (naive Bayes classifiers, decision trees, support vector machines, and neural networks) and the modalities to evaluate their performance. Examples of specific applications of algorithms are given using System R. © Springer International Publishing Switzerland 2015.
