AB  - The proceedings contain 28 papers. The topics discussed include: detecting accounting frauds in publicly traded U.S. firms: a machine learning approach; improving Sybil detection via graph pruning and regularization techniques; class-prior estimation for learning from positive and unlabeled data; curriculum learning of Bayesian network structure; expectation propagation for rectified linear Poisson regression; preference relation-based Markov random fields for recommender systems; surrogate regret bounds for generalized classification performance metrics; streaming variational inference for Dirichlet process mixtures; continuous target shift adaptation in supervised learning; proximal average approximated incremental gradient method for composite penalty regularized empirical risk minimization; a unified framework for jointly learning distributed representations of word and attributes; regularized policy gradients: direct variance reduction in policy gradient estimation; budgeted bandit problems with continuous random costs; statistical unfolded logic learning; and integration of single-view graphs with diffusion of tensor product graphs for multi-view spectral clustering.
