AB  - Learning classifiers from imbalanced data has attracted a significant amount of interest in recent years. The imbalanced class in the dataset problem is a special type of classification problem where the class priors are highly unequal and imbalanced. Resampling ensemble algorithm is developed focused on the classification problems for imbalanced datasets. The small classes are over sampled by the use of SMOTE (Synthetic Minority Oversampling Technique) algorithm and large classes are under- sampled where the samples are to be selected randomly from the majority class data. The optimization technique has been introduced on the oversampling and undersampling process in imbalanced classification. The aim is to study the use of Optimization Technique to improve the performance of imbalanced classification. A novel approach called as BAT Algorithm for over and under sampling (BAOUS) technique where the accuracy rate of all the classes is optimized at the same time. From the experimental result, the system is used to reduce the time complexity as well as it will enhance the accuracy rate of the imbalance classification result. © Research India Publications.
