AB  - Accuracy is commonly used as an index to evaluate the performance of classifiers. However, accuracy has several deficiencies, such as the sensitivity to class prior distribution and misclassification costs. Especially in the disease diagnosis, the classifier selected according to accuracy is not necessarily the optimal classifier. While the Receiver Operating Characteristic Curve (ROC) and the Area Under ROC (AUC) analysis technology are insensitive to the class distribution and different misclassification cost. Besides, they have advantages of direct-viewing, and easy to understand. This experiment is testing and analyzing the UCI datasets (Parkinson, diabetes, liver-disorder, breast-cancer) using different classifiers (LDC, KNNC, SVC), and comparing with the general indicator, to find out the optimal classifier to each group of data sets. At the same time, experiment shows the advantages of ROC and AUC in the evaluation of medical decision-making. © 2013 ISSN 2185-2766.
