AB  - The aim of this paper is the Bayesian estimation techniques to obtain the form of the a posteriori density p(μ\D) and the desired probability density p(X\D) in the case when p(X\μ) ∼ N(μ ∑). The treatment of the multivariate case in which ∑ is known but μ is not represents the generalization of the univariate case (see [5]). This approach is then used in Bavesian classification. COPYRIGHT 2008 EUDOXUS PRESS, LLC.
