AB  - The proceedings contain 37 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Flexible Query Answering Systems. The topics include: WeLink: A Named Entity Disambiguation Approach for a QAS over Knowledge Bases; a Heuristic Pruning Technique for Dialectical Trees on Argumentation-Based Query-Answering Systems; a Method for Efficient Argument-Based Inquiry; DAQAP: Defeasible Argumentation Query Answering Platform; an Efficient Algorithm for Computing the Set of Semi-stable Extensions; using Word Embeddings and Deep Learning for Supervised Topic Detection in Social Networks; generalized Association Rules for Sentiment Analysis in Twitter; Data Exploration in the HIFUN Language; reducing Skyline Query Results: An Approach Based on Fuzzy Satisfaction of Concepts; Personal Big Data, GDPR and Anonymization; quantify the Variability of Time Series of Imprecise Data; semantic Understanding of Natural Language Stories for Near Human Question Answering; deductive Querying of Natural Logic Bases; clustering of Intercriteria Analysis Data Using a Health-Related Quality of Life Data; a Flexible Query Answering System for Movie Analytics; can BlockChain Technology Provide Information Systems with Trusted Database? The Case of HyperLedger Fabric; anticipating Depression Based on Online Social Media Behaviour; method for Modeling and Simulation of Parallel Data Integration Processes in Wireless Sensor Networks; find the Right Peers: Building and Querying Multi-IoT Networks Based on Contexts; handling Veracity of Nominal Data in Big Data: A Multipolar Approach; tutorial: Supervised Learning for Prevalence Estimation; interCriteria Analysis with Interval-Valued Intuitionistic Fuzzy Evaluations; business Dynamism and Innovation Capability in the European Union Member States in 2018 Through the Prism of InterCriteria Analysis.
