AB  - The proceedings contain 61 papers. The topics discussed include: retrieval in CBR using a combination of similarity and association knowledge; a clustering approach using weighted similarity majority margins; a method for finding groups of related herbs in traditional Chinese medicine; a new hybrid clustering method for reducing very large spatio-temporal dataset; a normal distribution-based over-sampling approach to imbalanced data classification; a probabilistic topic model with social tags for query reformulation in informational search; bi-clustering gene expression data using co-similarity; generating syntactic tree templates for feature-based opinion mining; handling concept drift via ensemble and class distribution estimation technique; hybrid artificial immune algorithm and CMAC neural network classifier for supporting business and medical decision making; and individual doctor recommendation model on medical social network.
