AB  - Alzheimer’s disease (AD) is characterized by amyloidosis of brain tissues. This phenomenon is studied with genetically-modiﬁed mouse models. We propose a method to quantify amyloidosis in whole 5x FAD mouse brains, a model of AD. We use optical projection tomography (OPT) and a random forest voxel classiﬁer to segment and measure amyloid plaques. We validate our method in a preliminary cross-sectional study, where we measure 6136±1637, 8477±3438, and 17267±4241 plaques (AVG±SD) at 11, 17, and 31 weeks. Overall, this method can be used in the evaluation of new treatments against AD. © 2019 Optical Society of America under the terms of the OSA Open Access Publishing Agreement.
