AB  - The proceedings contain 173 papers. The topics discussed include: diffusion-based Bayesian cluster enumeration in distributed sensor networks; a distributed transmission scheduling algorithm for wireless networks based on the ising model; on convergence analysis of gradient based primal-dual method of multipliers; dempster-shafer theory based robust sequential detection in distributed sensor networks; generalized adaptive weighted recursive least squares dictionary learning for retinal vessel inpainting; the statistical restricted isometry property for Gabor systems; a network compatibility condition for compressed sensing over complex networks; coupled compressive sensing: sequential reinforcement approach; least-squares based layerwise pruning of convolutional neural networks; learning DAGs using multiclass support vector machines; edge consensus computing for heterogeneous data sets; differential privacy for positive and unlabeled learning with known class priors; weakly supervised learning of multiple-scale dictionaries; wireless communication links as opportunistic IoT for near ground rain monitoring; tomographic reconstruction of rainfall fields using heterogeneous frequency microwave links; learning-based rainfall estimation via communication satellite links; a geometrical study of the bivariate fractional gaussian noise; and secrecy capacity analysis of transmit-receive diversity systems.
