AB  - This paper proposes a method for classifying ElectroEncephaloGraphic (EEG) signals for Brain-Computer Interface (BCI). BCI is a system that allows people with disabilities to interact directly or indirectly with their environment only by using brain activity. In this study, we present a model for classifying EEG signals from five different mental activities (converse, read, watch video, rest and work). The method of signal acquisition is non-invasive, resulting in significant data loss and artifacts that must be reduced. In order to do this, a quantification method using Fast Fourier Transform (FFT) and Root Mean Square (RMS) for feature extraction are applied to improve the quality of the signal reception. We propose an approach to the neural network Self-Organizing Map (SOM) to classify these filtered signals. © 2018 IEEE.
